"comparison": "Both NVDA and AMD disclose specific unconditional purchase commitments for inventory components (NVDA for inventory/manufacturing capacity, AMD for wafers and substrates) at the end of fiscal year 2024. NVDA emphasizes that these commitments were impacted by 'shortening lead times' and highlights the risk of incurring inventory provisions if commitments exceed demand. In contrast, AMD provides a precise monetary quantification of its obligations ($5.0 billion total, with $4.5 billion due in FY2025) and notes that it actively manages payment and delivery timing with suppliers based on business conditions, rather than explicitly stating the commitments were driven by lead time changes in this specific disclosure segment.",
